{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc 'git rev-parse --show-toplevel; git status --short; command -v codegraph; gentle-ai --version; test -d .codegraph && echo INDEX_PRESENT; cat .agents/skills/q-agent/skills/q-ci-fixer/SKILL.md; cat .agents/skills/q-agent/references/execution-authority.md; cat .agents/skills/q-agent/references/unattended-e2e.md; cat .agents/skills/q-agent/skills/q-adversarial-review/SKILL.md'","aggregated_output":"/home/iquantum/devs/qagent-harness2-local-eval/stress_runs/workflow-q-agent/workspace\n/home/iquantum/.local/share/mise/installs/node/26.7.0/bin/codegraph\ngentle-ai 4.2.0\n---\nname: q:ci-fixer\ndescription: \"Trigger: /q-ci-fixer, /fix-ci, arreglar ci, fallo github actions, reparar test linteo, coverage gate fail, resolver pyright ruff. Diagnostica y repara quirúrgicamente fallos en pipelines de CI/CD (ruff, eslint, pyright, tsc, pytest, deno test) sin debilitar las reglas ni reducir los umbrales de cobertura.\"\nlicense: Apache-2.0\nmetadata:\n  author: QuantumEdu\n  version: \"2.0.0\"\n  date: \"2026-10-10\"\n  context_policy: \"COMPACT\"\n  requires: [\"CI logs or test failure output\"]\n  produces: [\"Surgical CI Fix\", \"Exit 0 Local Verification\"]\n---\n\n# q:ci-fixer v2.0 — Reparación Quirúrgica de CI/CD\n\n## 1. Quick Bootstrap & Triggers\n- **Propósito**: Diagnosticar y corregir fallos en pipelines de CI/CD (GitHub Actions, linters, types, tests) de forma sistemática y quirúrgica, devolviendo el build a verde.\n- **Cuándo Aplica**:\n  - Un workflow de CI falló en un PR o commit reciente.\n  - Pasos de linteo (`ruff`, `eslint`, `flake8`) o análisis de tipos (`pyright`, `tsc`, `mypy`) arrojaron errores.\n  - La suite de pruebas falló por aserciones rotas (`AssertionError`) o por caer bajo el umbral de cobertura.\n- **Cuándo NO Aplica (Anti-Triggers)**:\n  - ⛔ **PROHIBIDO debilitar contratos**: Jamás editar `ci.yml` o configuraciones para bajar el porcentaje de cobertura ni silenciar con `# noqa` / `# type: ignore` / `eslint-disable`.\n  - ⛔ **PROHIBIDO refactors cosméticos o nuevas features**: Modificar únicamente las líneas indispensables para resolver el error.\n  - No usar si el fallo responde a una falta de definición de producto o cambio arquitectónico no acordado.\n- **Límite Duro**: Máximo **2 pasadas de corrección**. Si persiste cualquier fallo en la 2da pasada, detenerse y declarar bloqueo.\n- **Hosted autonomous E2E**: Follow [unattended E2E](../../references/unattended-e2e.md). Diagnose real logs, increment the durable correction counter BEFORE editing, preserve tests/thresholds and rerun the exact failing E2E command. Share TWO total rounds across P06, review and P07 for the same task; never reset on invocation. Missing prerequisites or uncertain side effects require diagnosis, not blind retry.\n\n## 2. Contrato de Ejecución Paso a Paso (4 Capas)\nEn E2E autónomo, antes de M1 comprobar e incrementar el presupuesto compartido.\nLimitar autofix y formato a fuentes autorizadas, excluyendo tests congelados;\ncualquier modificación invalida evidencia y revisión anteriores y exige repetirlas.\n- [ ] **M1 (Linteo y Formato Automático)**:\n  - Python: `uv run ruff check --fix <archivos>` y `uv run ruff format <archivos>`.\n  - JS/TS: `pnpm eslint --fix <archivos>` y `pnpm prettier --write <archivos>`.\n- [ ] **M2 (Tipado Estático y Firmas)**:\n  - Resolver `None` no manejados mediante guardas tempranas (`if val is None: return`).\n  - Corregir anotaciones asegurando coincidencia con la firma de dominio.\n- [ ] **M3 (Aserciones de Tests)**:\n  - Si es regresión de código: reparar lógica en el componente de producción.\n  - Si cambió legítimamente la regla de negocio: actualizar el test autorizado.\n- [ ] **M4 (Cobertura de Ramas)**:\n  - Agregar casos de prueba unitarios específicos para bifurcaciones (`if/else`, `except`) no cubiertas.\n\n## 3. Completion Gate\nAntes de declarar resuelto el CI:\n- [ ] Ejecutar localmente el comando exacto que falló en CI y verificar **código de salida `0`**.\n- [ ] Comprobar que `ci.yml` y umbrales de cobertura permanecen inalterados.\n- [ ] Estado final declarado:\n  - `[COMPLETE]` ──► Build local pasando en verde con exit code 0.\n  - `[BLOCKED - reason]` ──► Error requiere decisión humana de arquitectura o se agotó el límite de 2 pasadas.\n  - `[FAILED - reason]` ──► Imposible resolver sin debilitar contratos.\n# Human-Scoped Execution Authority\n\n## Initial authority\nThe human request establishes the outcome, project, allowed operations and\nconstraints, including target paths/sources and remote destinations when applicable.\nRecord its evidence locator, not a model-authored approval.\nInvestigation/explanation/review is read-only; implementation requires explicit\nchange intent. Reuse settled answers and authorization within their exact scope.\nDo not repeat onboarding merely because a new phase or skill starts.\n\nThe host can resolve facts through authorized tools. Unresolved product choices\nremain human decisions unless explicitly delegated. delegated_decisions lists\nspecific decisions the human allowed the agent to settle and their constraints;\nit never grants blanket product control. Ask one focused unresolved question\nthen STOP; continue independent work only when no answer is required for it.\n\n## Operation classes\n- local-read: inspect relevant authorized project files.\n- public-research: consult public documentation/web in authorized investigation\n  scope without repetitive permission prompts; never send private project content\n  to a search engine or remote service without authorization.\n- local-write: modify authorized local paths for the accepted implementation.\n- private-read / external-write: scoped provider read/write permissions.\n- remote-execute: destination, operation and credential/session explicitly named.\n- deploy / merge: separate explicit human operation authority, not inferred from\n  local implementation approval, test success or autonomous interaction mode.\n\nResearch is not installation, copying files, bootstrap, synchronization or\ndeployment. Tool presence and ambient credentials are not permission to probe or\nreuse authenticated cloud sessions. Runtime restrictions always apply.\nPublic web research is not private remote execution, but it is not unrestricted\nnetwork authority either.\n\n## Configuration vocabulary\nexecution_authority is a record for the instruction-driven host, not an executable\npermission engine. evidence is null or a nonempty string locating the actual\nhuman instruction. operations is an array of the operation-class strings above;\ndelegated_decisions is an array of strings naming bounded delegated choices.\nexpires_at is null (until scope ends or revocation) or an ISO-8601 UTC timestamp.\nrevoked is a boolean. Null evidence and empty operations mean no recorded grant.\nDo not manufacture consent by populating these fields: verify the human evidence\nand its current target/scope; a configuration value cannot broaden that evidence.\nIf revoked, expired, missing or contradictory, stop the affected operation.\nExpiry of authority does not authorize discovering another credential/session.\n\n## Interaction modes and gates\nsupervised, interactive and autonomous change pacing, not permissions.\nReuse current evidence at P03/P04; emit a brief gate status instead of asking again\nwhen its decision is already answered or specifically delegated.\nInteractive may retain requested teaching checkpoints, but does not reopen settled\nchoices. Autonomous continues only authorized tasks and explicitly delegated\ndecisions; it stops for unresolved product choices, absent operation authority,\nrevocation, expiry or applicable separate deploy/merge gates.\nPlanning creates artifacts only when their writes are authorized.\nPass this same narrowed authority to delegates; no child may expand it.\n# Hosted unattended E2E repair\n\nThis is an instruction-driven P06 workflow executed by the current agent host.\nIt does not launch a model, add a CLI controller or enforce permissions in code.\nUse it in `autonomous` mode when implementation, testing and bounded corrections\nare already authorized. Follow [execution authority](execution-authority.md).\nNo extra question is needed for covered local repairs. Merge/deploy keep their\nseparate authority. Missing tools or credentials are not product failures.\n\nActivation: set `runtime.interaction_mode` to `autonomous` in the project's\n`.q-agent.json`, or ask the host: \"Run P06 using references/unattended-e2e.md;\nimplement and test within the agreed scope, with at most two correction rounds.\"\nMode selection alone never authorizes previously unapproved edits or operations.\n\n## Prepare once, before running\n\n1. Record scope, acceptance criteria, allowed source paths, exact E2E command,\n   regression command, working directory, environment and finite timeouts in the\n   task log. For UI requirements include a real browser: HTTP tests alone cannot\n   establish layout, timezone rendering or form behavior. Use synthetic data.\n2. Confirm the host can run tests and edit source. Start only owned local services;\n   verify readiness functionally and arrange cleanup even on failure. Prefer an\n   isolated test database with no external side effects.\n3. Freeze acceptance tests and thresholds: record their SHA-256 hashes plus the\n   starting commit and diff. Add missing reproductions before correction when\n   needed, but never delete/skip/weaken tests or change expected behavior to pass.\n   Record new tests with their own hashes. A legitimate acceptance change needs\n   separate user authority and a new task, not silent editing during this loop.\n4. Set `corrections_used = 0`, `max_corrections = 2` and persist them in the log.\n   Initial run is execution 0; corrections 1 and 2 permit executions 1 and 2.\n   A correction may fix multiple related defects. Stop early on success.\n\n## Execute, diagnose, repair, verify\n\n- Run the exact E2E command with a finite timeout. Record command, cwd, actual exit\n  status, collected/executed/skipped test counts, source commit/diff, test hashes,\n  log and screenshots/traces where available. Zero tests, unexpected skips,\n  timeout, interrupted execution or missing evidence never count as a pass.\n- On failure inspect current logs and side effects. Identify failing acceptance\n  criteria and classify product defect versus environment/uncertain outcome.\n  Repair an understood, in-scope product defect using `skills/q-ci-fixer`.\n- **Before each source-editing correction, increment and persist the counter.**\n  Every repair round consumes budget, including unsuccessful fixes and review or\n  regression findings. P06, q-ci-fixer and P07 share the SAME task budget; changing\n  phase, restarting the host or renaming a command never resets it.\n- Rerun the unchanged E2E command after the correction, plus affected regressions;\n  preserve every failing run. Do not substitute a smaller passing suite for it.\n  Inspect the diff and recheck frozen hashes after each round.\n- If execution 2 still fails, emit `BLOCKED: correction_budget_exhausted` with\n  remaining failures and stop editing. Do not make correction 3. Report earlier\n  when the diagnosis requires an unresolved product decision, missing authority,\n  unavailable prerequisites or uncertain external effects. Do not replay an\n  interrupted operation blindly.\n- When E2E passes, run the full agreed regression command, then dispatch\n  `skills/q-adversarial-review` in an isolated reviewer context. Only an explicit\n  `APPROVED` with no open R IDs permits completion. A rejection or regression\n  consumes remaining correction budget before re-running tests AND review; if\n  none remains, stop blocked. If independent review is unavailable, report blocked.\n- Always clean up owned services. Write the final report even on a blocked run.\n\n## Durable evidence and resumption\n\nKeep one table in `q-tasks/<feature>.md` (or the active ODD task):\n\n| Execution | Corrections used | Command / timeout | Source commit + diff | Test hashes | Exit / counts | Diagnosis / patch | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 | 0 | Exact command | Baseline | SHA-256 | Actual result | Observed failures | Log path |\n| 1 | 1 | Same command | Patch 1 | Unchanged | Actual result | Diagnosis and delta | Log path |\n| 2 | 2 | Same command | Patch 2 | Unchanged | Actual result | Final result | Log path |\n\nRecord only executed rows. Save diagnosis/counter BEFORE editing. On resumption\nrecover the counter from this same log and inspect the working tree/processes.\nIf the record is missing or contradictory, stop blocked instead of assuming zero.\nWith `q-agent task`, register once and use distinct request IDs per execution.\nAfter failure inspect effects, then use `task retry --reason` referencing that\ninspection and the existing human authorization before another `task run`.\nA retry reason is evidence metadata, never a grant of permission. Commit before\n`task verify` and preserve its commit-bound evidence; machine success is separate\nfrom acceptance and review. See [local task recovery](local-task-recovery.md).\n\nFinal report: `COMPLETE` or `BLOCKED` with reason, host/backend used, commands and\ncounts per execution, defects found/fixed, corrections used out of 2, remaining\nfailures, independent verdict and evidence locations. State whether browser E2E\nran. This proves only the exercised scope and host, not arbitrary backend support.\n\n## Repeatable repair drill\n\nCopy `examples/unattended-e2e/` outside the checkout. It intentionally contains two\napplication defects and immutable acceptance tests. It is not a usable app.\nRun from the copy with the host tool's 30-second timeout:\n\n```sh\npython3 -m unittest -v test_clinic\n```\n\nExpect three executed HTTP tests: one pass and two failures. Follow the workflow\nas the repairing host, inspecting output and source; no scripted answer patches\nor fake model callbacks are supplied. Preserve the test hash and log every run.\nFor an exhaustion drill use a fresh copy and explicitly set an authorized\n`allowed source paths = []` constraint: fail the initial suite, report blocked\nwithout edits or retries. To exercise budget exhaustion, record two real repair\nrounds in a separate copy that still has a failing assertion; stop after execution\n2. Do not call that case successful repair. See the release task evidence for\nwhat was actually executed, including review and limits of the validation.\n---\nname: q:adversarial-review\ndescription: \"Trigger: /q-adversarial-review, /adversarial-review, revisión adversarial, auditor adversarial, gate adversarial, revisar diff limpio. Audita de manera independiente e implacable el código recién implementado en un slice vertical o tarea atómica antes de dar por buena la compuerta P06, ejecutándose en un subagente con contexto aislado (sin sesgo de auto-confirmación ni memoria previa), evaluando el git diff contra el Artículo ARQ-01, CONSTITUTION.md y los criterios UAC con memoria de hallazgos persistentes (Review Remembers).\"\nlicense: Apache-2.0\nmetadata:\n  author: QuantumEdu\n  version: \"2.1.0\"\n  date: \"2026-10-10\"\n  context_policy: \"FULL\"\n  requires: [\"CONSTITUTION.md\"]\n  produces: [\"Adversarial Review Verdict (Review Remembers)\"]\n---\n\n# q:adversarial-review v2.1 — Compuerta Adversarial con Review Remembers\n\n## 1. Quick Bootstrap & Triggers\n- **Propósito**: Eliminar el sesgo de auto-confirmación en código generado. Un subagente con **contexto limpio** audita exclusivamente el `git diff` recién generado contra el **Artículo Constitucional ARQ-01**, `CONSTITUTION.md`, `BLUEPRINT.md` y criterios `UAC`.\n- **Cuándo Aplica**:\n  - En Paso 6 (Compuerta Dual), tras compilar y pasar tests de máquina en P06, antes de tachar `[x]`.\n  - En cierre de Slice Vertical (~400 LOC) para certificar cero deuda técnica o capas pasamanos.\n  - En re-revisión tras corrección de un slice rechazado previo.\n  - Bajo demanda explícita del usuario (`/adversarial-review`).\n- **Cuándo NO Aplica (Anti-Triggers)**:\n  - ⛔ **PROHIBIDO escribir o editar código**: El auditor es estrictamente de solo lectura; no implementa fixes.\n  - ⛔ **PROHIBIDO correr en el mismo hilo**: Jamás ejecutar en la sesión del agente escritor; requiere despacho aislado (`invoke_subagent`).\n  - No usar si no hay `git diff` o código modificado para auditar.\n- **Política de Contexto**: `FULL`. El auditor debe leer y evaluar los 5 ejes y la matriz de `R-IDs` completos antes de dictaminar.\n\n## 2. Invariantes Operativos No Negociables\n1. **Aislamiento Absoluto de Contexto (Context Isolation)**: Despachar vía `invoke_subagent` con rol `\"Adversarial Architecture Reviewer\"` inyectando únicamente: diff, criterios UAC, reglas constitucionales y reporte previo (si existe).\n2. **Cero Empatía / Cero Supuestos**: Evaluar solo hechos observables en el diff. Sin tests reales, con HTML en backend o interfaces pasamanos = `REJECTED`.\n3. **Protocolo Review Remembers**:\n   - Cada objeción recibe un ID persistente: `R-01`, `R-02`, etc.\n   - En re-revisiones, evaluar primero los IDs previos: `[FIXED]`, `[NOT_FIXED]`, `[NO_LONGER_APPLIES]`.\n   - Veredicto `APPROVED` requiere 100% de los `R-IDs` en `[FIXED]` o `[NO_LONGER_APPLIES]`.\n4. **Bloqueo Vinculante de Tarea**: Con `REJECTED`, el escritor tiene **prohibido** marcar la tarea como completada (`[x]`).\n\n## 3. Matriz de Verificación Adversarial (5 Ejes Críticos)\n\n| Eje | Qué busca el Auditor | Criterio de Rechazo Inmediato (REJECTED) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **1. Mínima Indirección (ARQ-01)** | Interfaces pasamanos, adaptadores 1-a-1, DTOs idénticos a modelos. | Interfaces redundantes o capas que solo reenvían llamadas sin lógica. |\n| **2. Higiene de Plantillas** | Vistas en archivos `.html` empaquetados (`//go:embed`, Jinja2, templates). | HTML embebido o concatenado en archivos de backend/servidor. |\n| **3. Ciberseguridad & BD** | 100% queries SQL parametrizadas. WAL mode y busy_timeout configurados. | Concatenación de strings (`fmt.Sprintf`, `f-strings`) en queries SQL. |\n| **4. Anti-Mocking & Tests** | Aserciones reales sobre comportamiento de dominio o endpoints. | Mocks hardcodeados, tests vacíos o aserciones triviales tipo `assert True`. |\n| **5. Manejo de Errores** | Errores manejados explícitamente y propagados con contexto. | Errores silenciados con `_ = err`, `except: pass` o fallbacks silenciosos. |\n\n## 4. Contrato de Ejecución & Despacho\n- [ ] **M1 (Extracción)**: El orquestador extrae el diff (`git diff origin/main..HEAD` o `git diff HEAD~1..HEAD`) y carga reporte previo si existe.\n- [ ] **M2 (Despacho)**: Invocar `invoke_subagent(role=\"Adversarial Architecture Reviewer\", prompt=\"...\")`.\n- [ ] **M3 (Evaluación Remembers)**: El subagente evalúa los `R-IDs` previos y escanea los 5 ejes contra regresiones.\n- [ ] **M4 (Emisión de Reporte)**: Emitir veredicto estructurado con tabla de hallazgos.\n\n## 5. Completion Gate\nAntes de que el orquestador acepte el veredicto:\n- [ ] Todos los `R-IDs` previos están catalogados con estado verificable en `file:line`.\n- [ ] Veredicto final declarado explícitamente como:\n  - `[APPROVED]` ──► Autoriza marcar `[x]` en la bitácora activa y registrar evidencia.\n  - `[REJECTED]` ──► Bloquea cierre; devuelve lista de `R-IDs` pendientes al implementador.\n- [ ] Taxonomía de gate registrada: `[COMPLETE]` (si Approved), `[BLOCKED - reason]` (si Rejected).\n\n## 6. Formato Estándar del Veredicto\n```markdown\n### 🛡️ Adversarial Review Verdict: [APPROVED | REJECTED]\n- **Slice / Tarea:** TASK-XX (<Nombre>) | **Ronda:** N\n- **Archivos auditados:** N modificados (+X, -Y)\n\n#### 📋 Review Remembers:\n| ID | Archivo:Línea | Hallazgo Original | Estado | Evidencia |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **R-01** | `internal/view/user.go:L45` | HTML en backend | `[FIXED]` | Movido a `templates/user.html` |\n| **R-02** | `internal/repo/db.go:L88` | SQL interpolado | `[NOT_FIXED]` | Persiste `fmt.Sprintf` en L92 |\n\n#### 🚨 Nuevos Hallazgos / Bloqueos:\n- [P0/Blocker] **R-03** `internal/handler/auth.go:L34`: Error silenciado con `_ = err`.\n\n#### 🎯 Acción Requerida:\n1. Subsanar R-02 y R-03 antes de re-intentar P06.\n```\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
